<%#
  Rendered both from the controller, for an answer already in the cache, and
  from the job, which broadcasts it over the turn's own channel. The id has to
  match the pending bubble it replaces.

  The prompt asks for prose and forbids headings, lists and tables, so there is
  no markup to render and no renderer to reach for — simple_format splits the
  paragraphs and that is all that is wanted.

  It is given escaped text and told not to sanitise, rather than handed the raw
  string. simple_format sanitises by default, which strips a <script> but passes
  an <a href> straight through: a model that emitted one would put a live
  outbound link on the page. The no-markup rule is a prompt-level guarantee, and
  a prompt-level guarantee is the wrong thing to leave holding this.
%>
<article id="<%= turn.dom_id %>" class="space-y-4 text-stone-300">
  <%= simple_format(h(answer), { class: "text-[1.0625rem] leading-7" }, sanitize: false) %>
</article>
